I'm so going to hell - one way or another.

I've been playing for about 6 months now - (and many thanks to this
fine group for all the pointers, tips and resources) - and I've never
had a game start this good. No ascensions as yet - I've yet to see the
Amulet.

Been playing barbarians and wizards - cranked up a monk last night -
and I still don't believe how well it's going. The RNG has GOT to be
saving up something nasty - or I'll YASD somewhere but...

Found a broad pick right next to me when I started and cracked open a
vault on the way down to the next level. Level 2 I find a large
general store, price ID a few things and then let the dog steal it
blind. Price tested clear potion and identify scroll yielded some
scroll identification and enough left to identify the ring as sustain
ability. Sold the nasty scrolls and rolled on.

Nothing much on 3 - 4 had a small bookstore that after the doggie did
his thing yeilded 2 scrolls of ID and a few spellbooks. Read a scroll
of ID - boom. Did the lot. Sold the dig, slow monster, haste self and
cause fear, successfully learned the healing, magic missile and force
bolt - rolled on after dumping the glass beads.

5 was clear of anything much beyond a couple packs of hill orcs -
rolled on to 6. Here's where the blinking started...stumbled over a
white unicorn which gratefully took my two obsidian stones for a
little luck building - then I found a 6 critter throne room. Cleaned
it out and after setting my gold aside sat down. Out of Place - then a
wish. Went for the +2 blessed rustproof GoP - got them - throne still
there. Followed it up with a genocide (chose dwarves, looking at the
mines ahead) and then boosted the HP before vanishing. Rolled on to
the stairs - and hacked open another vault on the way.

7. First 'bad' luck - a pack of four winter wolf cubs nuked most of my
potions - but I did get a magic whistle as a consolation. On to 8 -
and at the end of it, I'm really starting to wonder. Found a chest
with a ring, scroll of ID and a spellbook. Scroll of ID does entire
inventory - Ring of Protection +1 and spellbook of Detect Unseen.
Found another throne room - much heavier population but sneaky monk
and dog manage to do the business. sit down after setting gold aside -
electric shock. Then - another wish. Ring of SD thank you - still
vegetarian and that will help - low on food. Stumble over a grey
unicorn on the way to the down stairs and get a horn.

9 is the Oracle. One cursed spellbook in the bunch of statues - dump
it. Do tame a second dog. Down to 10 where find Sokoban entrance - and
a non-cursed copy of the spellbook that was cursed the level above.
Hold off on even attempting to read though.

Sokoban - Lose 1 dog on the way up and have to bust 1 boulder. Nearly
got creamed in the final big brawl room but healing spell and dog and
I pull through. AoR - and a pair of elven helms. Pet testing shows
both safe - one turns out to be +2. By this stage I have a +3 robe to
go with the GoP...I'm starting to worry. Four rings and a couple
non-ID'd wands as well through the whole Sokoban thing - and food is
no longer an issue.

Head off to the mines - find a lamp on the first corpse of a gnome and
pet testing shows safe - find two more on the level. And a cloak of
displacement - can't use it with the robe but even so... then hammer
through pretty easy - next level is lit and nothing remotely
threatening on either.

Mine Town - and here's where the RNG is really making me wonder what
NASTY it's got coming...

Co-aligned altar. Thanks to my using healing spell on him the dog
takes out a captain and three watchmen - selling thier gear let me buy
two lots of protection from the priest for a nekkid AC 6. Izchak turns
out to have a magic lamp and the general store yeilds an expensive
bag. Holy water prayer, bless the scroll of ID - Yup. It's a magic
lamp. Bless it. Oilskin sack not BoH but I'm not complaining at all.
Bless that to boot. Exit temple - and walk into a black unicorn.
Sacrifice offer - walk out. Stumble into a grey unicorn. Repeat.
Izchak only has 5 candles in the store - but otherwise I'm sitting
pretty...and I can't help but think the RNG is SO going to get me for
this.

Two questions folks - I know it's rare to get a game that just...I'm
paraniod enough right now I'm taking a minute to think about EVERY
move to avoid a YASD...and waiting for the other shoe to drop. Am I
right in thinking it's gotta turn around on me with a vengeance the
other way - the RNG keep track and 'balance out' you find even if not
in the code?

Save the magic lamp - (which is my intention at this point) - or
whistle up the BoS?

Thanks again for the great resource - I'll keep you posted. I'm going
to bed now to soothe my nerves (and so I play fresh tomorrow..)

